Z||000000||Cooter||11-13-1999||08:54 PM||||I dug my copy of desk top dyno out of the closet and got it installed again. I was going to play around with the 2.8 engine and see what would happen. But, I cant recall the engine spec's right off the top of my head. So- I need the bore/stroke, intake and exhaust valve sizes and if anybody can post the specs on their cam, I will try to get them into the program to see what they show. I will need all the info from the "cam card" such as lift at .050, intake and exhaust valve opening and closing degrees, etc. . .<P>Thanks-<BR>Greg||||reg||3
Z||000001||batboy||11-13-1999||11:21 PM||||Cooter, sounds like you have an older version of Desktop Dyno like I originally had. My current Dyno version 2.8.7M has most of the common 4, 6, and 8 cylinder bore and stroke specs on the menu. There is a new version that was just recently released, Dyno2000. They are offering registered users a special price of $39.95 and comes with a total of 3 software packages: Dyno2000, a cool drag strip simulation program, and Hotrod Magazine's computer drag racing game called Burnout Pro.<P>Anyway, the specs you'll need to plug in for the 2.8L engine are: bore=3.5", stroke=3.0", compression ratio=8.9:1 (I use 9:1 since there is no 8.9 option in the program), intake valves=1.72", and exhaust valves=1.42" (HO heads). There are two factory cams that are listed for the 2.8, one for base S-10/Camaros and a high performance cam that I assume is the one the Fiero uses since it's a HO 2.8 engine. Cam specs for the high performance factory 2.8 cam are: lift=.394/.410, duration @ 0.050"=196/203 degrees, and lobe centerline=109 degrees (I have no lobe-centerline data).<P>The specs for the GM 3.4 HO cam that a lot of people are rebuilding their 2.8/3.1 engines with are: lift=.426/.454 and duration at 0.050" 204/216 degrees. Most performance cams usually have a 110 degree lobe-center angle and 106 degree intake centerline. Most major cam companies also post their cam specs on the internet now. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||11-13-1999||11:26 PM||||These are from an 86 helms<BR>bore              89<BR>stroke            76<BR>lift intake       5.87/6.67<BR>     exhaust      6.67/6.94<BR>valve dia. intake 1.25/1.50<BR>          exhaust 1.60/1.90<BR>rocker ratio      1.5||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||11-14-1999||12:53 PM||||Tom, I believe those specs you listed are in metric, at least I know the bore and stroke you gave is correct in millimeters. Unfortunately, I don't think this computer program that Cooter is talking about uses metric measurements.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tim||11-14-1999||01:03 PM||||Divide mm by 25.4 = inches||||reg||1
